AC14: tools/eslint.config.js may gain only a block with files and languageOptions.globals. This is checked through ESLint’s own effective config, from tools/:
- `find src test -name '*.js' | xargs -n 1 npx eslint --print-config | jq -S -c .rules | sort -u | shasum -a 256` must be 856ee00120171941ee04ed2318fd4d5a4264a59fcff999b4fb5a1b22f695be08 (one rules line for all files);
- the globals of files outside public/ must hash to bec0f88d493c5af9403051ad0ff2c4216dbab9ca43f4f5fbf7fedb8934b825bd;
- the old word grep stays, for ignores.
Unlike a grep, this catches numeric severities: the validator’s `"no-undef": 0` changes the rules hash. xargs -n 1 replaces -exec … \; because a bare backslash would break the YAML double-quoted string. Dry runs are in the summary.
